# Store every text file with LF in the repository and check it out as LF on
# every platform.
#
# Without this, git's core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default) rewrites working
# copies to CRLF. The blobs stay LF, so nothing breaks for a solo developer on
# one machine — but a clone on another OS, or a tool that compares the working
# tree rather than the index, sees whole files as changed.
#
# text=auto lets git detect and leave binary files alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
